      "What affects LED TV screen replacement cost in Delhi?",
      "The main factors are TV size, brand, panel type, model age, physical damage, part availability and whether the display glass is cracked. Large panels usually cost more and some older models may not have practical panel availability. If the panel is physically cracked or internally damaged, replacement may be expensive. If the symptom is sound with no picture, weak brightness or flickering, a backlight or board-level diagnosis may be more relevant than screen replacement.",
      "Screen damage versus backlight or board fault",
      "A physically cracked screen is different from a dark screen. Backlight failure can make the TV look black while sound continues. T-Con or mainboard issues can create lines, half display or unstable picture. Power board faults can stop the set from turning on. GR Solution checks these possibilities before suggesting screen replacement because replacing a panel without diagnosis can waste money.",
      "When is replacement not worth it?",
      "Replacement may not be worth it when the panel cost is close to a new TV, when parts are unavailable, when the TV is very old, or when multiple faults are present. Repair may be worth checking when the screen glass is intact and the fault is likely backlight, power, audio, HDMI, T-Con or motherboard related.",
      "What to check before calling",
      "Check whether sound is present, whether the standby light appears, whether the screen has visible cracks, whether menus are visible, and whether the problem appears on every input. Share the brand, model number, screen size, Delhi location and a clear photo or video of the symptom.",
